1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,522
In Class 1, everything on your map was on one side, and it was yours.

2
00:00:07,422 --> 00:00:09,596
Today the map gets politics.

3
00:00:10,496 --> 00:00:12,670
These people want your hulk,

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:16,163
and these people will fix your ship.

5
00:00:17,963 --> 00:00:21,007
That's three short records in your file,

6
00:00:21,457 --> 00:00:25,370
and one line that says who is whose enemy.

7
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:30,048
You read these three lines in Lecture 11.

8
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:34,426
They make a side called t s n,

9
00:00:34,876 --> 00:00:38,789
and they give it a name and a color.

10
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:43,167
Now look where else that word turns up.

11
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:47,111
It's on the line for DS 1,

12
00:00:47,561 --> 00:00:50,604
it's on the line for the hulk,

13
00:00:51,054 --> 00:00:53,228
and it's on your tug.

14
00:00:55,028 --> 00:00:59,376
Inside the quote marks, the first word is the side,

15
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:02,870
and the words after it are roles.

16
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:08,552
So t s n is the key of your own side.

17
00:01:09,002 --> 00:01:11,176
Hold on to that word.

18
00:01:12,976 --> 00:01:15,150
One more line, further down.

19
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:20,398
In Lecture 11 this one was marked for Class 2.

20
00:01:21,298 --> 00:01:25,646
It reads a section called sides from your fact sheet,

21
00:01:26,096 --> 00:01:28,704
and you haven't written one yet.

22
00:01:29,904 --> 00:01:31,643
So let's write one.

23
00:01:32,543 --> 00:01:36,457
Sides are records, like everything else in this file.

24
00:01:37,357 --> 00:01:40,835
The section is two hashes, the word Sides,

25
00:01:41,285 --> 00:01:46,937
and a key that has to be exactly that word, in small letters.

26
00:01:47,837 --> 00:01:50,446
Then one record for each side:

27
00:01:50,896 --> 00:01:53,939
three hashes, a name, and a key.

28
00:01:55,739 --> 00:01:57,913
My own side goes first,

29
00:01:58,363 --> 00:02:01,407
and its key is t s n,

30
00:02:01,857 --> 00:02:05,335
because that's the word my ship already carries.

31
00:02:06,235 --> 00:02:11,017
Then a color, which is a hash sign and three characters,

32
00:02:11,467 --> 00:02:13,641
for red, green and blue.

33
00:02:14,541 --> 00:02:19,324
Zero means none of it, and F means all of it.

34
00:02:20,224 --> 00:02:23,702
I save, I run lint, and it's clean.

35
00:02:24,902 --> 00:02:27,511
Now the people who aren't me.

36
00:02:28,411 --> 00:02:32,324
First the Breakers, with the key breaker, in orange.

37
00:02:33,224 --> 00:02:35,833
And here's the line that matters:

38
00:02:36,283 --> 00:02:38,457
Enemies, and then my key.

39
00:02:40,257 --> 00:02:44,604
Then the Harbor Guild, with the key guild, in green,

40
00:02:45,054 --> 00:02:48,098
and the line Allies, and my key.

41
00:02:48,998 --> 00:02:54,215
What comes after the colon is always a key, never a name.

42
00:02:55,115 --> 00:02:57,724
And I only say it once.

43
00:02:58,624 --> 00:03:02,102
Enemies on the Breakers makes them my enemy,

44
00:03:02,552 --> 00:03:04,726
and it makes me theirs.

45
00:03:05,176 --> 00:03:09,959
I don't go back and write it on my own record.

46
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:16,811
A side with nothing on it is just a name in a file.

47
00:03:17,711 --> 00:03:22,493
So I give each of them one thing on the map,

48
00:03:22,943 --> 00:03:28,596
and I do it with landmarks, the way you did in Lecture 10.

49
00:03:29,496 --> 00:03:33,409
A ship for the Breakers, out past the hulk,

50
00:03:33,859 --> 00:03:38,207
and a station for the Guild, west of DS 1.

51
00:03:39,107 --> 00:03:42,150
The Side line takes the side's key.

52
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:46,124
Now watch where I'm typing.

53
00:03:47,024 --> 00:03:50,067
These two go in the Landmarks section,

54
00:03:50,517 --> 00:03:52,257
above the Sides heading.

55
00:03:53,157 --> 00:03:56,635
If I type a landmark below that heading,

56
00:03:57,085 --> 00:04:01,433
the game reads it as a side called Breaker Cutter,

57
00:04:01,883 --> 00:04:04,491
and it puts no ship anywhere.

58
00:04:05,691 --> 00:04:09,170
Lecture 10 warned you about this next part.

59
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:13,548
My story ends with the words reach station.

60
00:04:14,448 --> 00:04:18,361
Station is a role, and every station wears it,

61
00:04:18,811 --> 00:04:21,854
and I've just built a second station.

62
00:04:22,754 --> 00:04:27,972
So the crew could carry the log to the Guild, and win.

63
00:04:29,772 --> 00:04:34,120
The cure is a role that only DS 1 wears.

64
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:38,063
In the step, I write reach home.

65
00:04:38,963 --> 00:04:42,441
Lint says nothing wears a role called home,

66
00:04:42,891 --> 00:04:46,370
which is true, because I'm only half done.

67
00:04:47,270 --> 00:04:52,052
So I go to line sixty-four, where DS 1 is made.

68
00:04:52,952 --> 00:04:55,561
Inside the quote marks, after station,

69
00:04:56,011 --> 00:05:00,359
I type a comma, a space, and the word home.

70
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:05,172
The side stays first, and the roles follow it.

71
00:05:06,072 --> 00:05:08,246
And now lint is clean.

72
00:05:09,446 --> 00:05:11,620
Three sides make three pairs.

73
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,128
Me and the Breakers are enemies,

74
00:05:15,578 --> 00:05:18,622
and me and the Guild are allies.

75
00:05:19,522 --> 00:05:24,304
But about the Breakers and the Guild, nobody said a word.

76
00:05:26,104 --> 00:05:30,452
And a pair nobody mentions is nothing to each other.

77
00:05:30,902 --> 00:05:32,641
The game doesn't guess.

78
00:05:33,541 --> 00:05:36,150
Scavengers and harbor pilots aren't strangers,

79
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:41,817
so I add the Guild's key after mine, with a comma between.

80
00:05:43,617 --> 00:05:46,661
So what does a relation buy you?

81
00:05:47,561 --> 00:05:51,039
An enemy reads as an enemy on Science,

82
00:05:51,489 --> 00:05:53,663
and Comms can taunt it.

83
00:05:54,563 --> 00:05:57,172
A friendly station lets you dock.

84
00:05:58,072 --> 00:06:02,854
And here's the one thing it doesn't buy you: a fight.

85
00:06:03,754 --> 00:06:08,102
The cutter has no orders, so it'll just sit there.

86
00:06:09,302 --> 00:06:11,911
Now let's break it on purpose.

87
00:06:12,811 --> 00:06:15,854
I misspell my own key after Enemies,

88
00:06:16,304 --> 00:06:18,043
and lint catches it.

89
00:06:18,943 --> 00:06:23,291
It says that word isn't a side in this mission,

90
00:06:23,741 --> 00:06:27,220
and it lists the keys I did declare.

91
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,759
But watch this one.

92
00:06:31,659 --> 00:06:35,572
I take the Side line off the cutter altogether,

93
00:06:36,022 --> 00:06:37,761
and lint says clean.

94
00:06:38,661 --> 00:06:43,878
And a fourth hash on the Guild's heading is clean as well.

95
00:06:45,678 --> 00:06:49,157
In the game, those two look the same.

96
00:06:50,057 --> 00:06:53,970
The thing reads as unknown on Science, for good,

97
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:57,898
and Comms has nothing to say to it.

98
00:06:58,798 --> 00:07:01,407
So when a contact stays unknown,

99
00:07:01,857 --> 00:07:04,465
look for its Side line first,

100
00:07:04,915 --> 00:07:08,393
and then count the hashes on its side.

101
00:07:09,593 --> 00:07:11,767
Here's the yard on Science.

102
00:07:12,667 --> 00:07:15,711
It's unknown until the scan is done,

103
00:07:16,161 --> 00:07:20,509
and then it's green, with the word guild beside it.

104
00:07:21,409 --> 00:07:23,583
On Comms I hail them,

105
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:27,946
and they tell me I have full docking privileges.

106
00:07:28,846 --> 00:07:30,585
And Helm can dock.

107
00:07:32,385 --> 00:07:34,124
Now the other one.

108
00:07:35,024 --> 00:07:38,502
It's red, with the word breaker beside it,

109
00:07:38,952 --> 00:07:41,996
and it reads enemy vessel, exercise caution.

110
00:07:42,896 --> 00:07:47,243
I hail it, and it tells me to go away.

111
00:07:48,143 --> 00:07:50,752
And then it just sits there,

112
00:07:51,202 --> 00:07:54,246
because being enemies doesn't start a fight.

113
00:07:56,046 --> 00:08:01,698
One last thing: I carry the log to the yard, and nothing happens.

114
00:08:02,598 --> 00:08:06,511
I carry it to DS 1, and we're home.

115
00:08:07,711 --> 00:08:13,363
Now it's your turn: write a faction of your own, with one ship.

116
00:08:14,263 --> 00:08:18,176
Say nothing about it, and Science calls it unknown.

117
00:08:19,076 --> 00:08:23,424
Give it a scan record, and it has a name.

118
00:08:24,324 --> 00:08:28,237
Then make it an enemy, and then a friend,

119
00:08:28,687 --> 00:08:31,296
and watch the name change color.

120
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:37,443
Next time, we meet the people who fly these ships.
